[{"text":"$LeviCivitaSign is a global variable that determines the sign in the result of a Dirac trace of four gamma matrices and \\gamma^5. $LeviCivitaSign is by default set to -1 which corresponds to the convention TR[LC[a,b,c,d,5]] = -4*I*Eps[a,b,c,d]. Setting $LeviCivitaSign=-I will switch to the FORM-convention.","anchor":"levicivitasign"},{"text":"Overview, LC, Eps, DiracTrace.","anchor":"see-also","section":"See also"},{"text":"$LeviCivitaSign DiracTrace[GA[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Rho], \\[Sigma], 5]] // DiracSimplify","anchor":"cb1","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-1\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[-4 i \\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\rho \\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"This sets the same convention as in FORM","anchor":"cb1-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"$LeviCivitaSign = -I; DiracTrace[GA[\\[Mu], \\[Nu], \\[Rho], \\[Sigma], 5]] // DiracSimplify","anchor":"cb2","section":"Examples"},{"text":"\\[4 \\bar{\\epsilon }^{\\mu \\nu \\rho \\sigma }\\]","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"Back to the standard value","anchor":"cb2-3","section":"Examples"},{"text":"$LeviCivitaSign = -1;","anchor":"cb3","section":"Examples"}]